                activity="Rock Climbing"
                activity_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-27T13:59:01.542-07:00"
                adventureType="Overnight Trip"
                adventureType_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-27T13:59:01.541-07:00"
                description="&lt;p>Colorado packs an unusual variety of rock into a small area: red sandstone, rough granite and smooth river-cut canyon walls, all within a day's drive. Over three days we climb on each of them and camp in between. The trip suits climbers who already lead outdoors and are comfortable on long days at altitude.&lt;/p>"
                description_x0040_ContentType="text/html"
                description_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-27T13:59:01.541-07:00"
                difficulty="Advanced"
                difficulty_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-27T13:59:01.543-07:00"
                gearList="&lt;ul>&#xa;&lt;li>Climbing shoes, harness and helmet&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>Sleeping bag and mat&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>Long trousers and shorts&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>A warm jacket for the evenings&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>Sun hat and sunscreen&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>Three litres of water capacity&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;/ul>"
                gearList_x0040_ContentType="text/html"
                gearList_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-27T13:59:01.545-07:00"
                groupSize="{Long}8"
                groupSize_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2022-05-27T14:51:12.873-07:00"
                itinerary="&lt;h2>Day 1: Sandstone&lt;/h2>&#xa;&lt;p>We begin among the red fins at the foot of the Front Range. The rock is soft and the holds are rounded, so the morning is a lesson in trusting your feet. Camp is an hour into the hills.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;h2>Day 2: Granite&lt;/h2>&#xa;&lt;p>A full day on a granite dome with routes of three to five pitches. Cracks, slabs and a summit wide enough to eat lunch on. We keep an eye on the sky: storms arrive in the early afternoon in summer, and we plan to be down before them.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;h2>Day 3: The canyon&lt;/h2>&#xa;&lt;p>The last morning is spent on shaded walls above a creek, on short, steep routes that are a pleasure after two long days. We finish with a late lunch in town.&lt;/p>"
                itinerary_x0040_ContentType="text/html"
